    "result_text": "The change is complete and the build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ownerSegment` field on the owner representation, formatted `<TIER>_<AREA>`.\n\n**`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added the `ownerSegment` property to the `Owner` schema as a read-only string enum (`PREMIUM_METRO`, `PREMIUM_REGIONAL`, `STANDARD_METRO`, `STANDARD_REGIONAL`), which generates `OwnerDto.OwnerSegmentEnum`.\n\n**`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping(target = \"ownerSegment\", ...)` on `toOwnerDto` and a `toOwnerSegment(Owner)` qualified mapping method that:\n- Sets TIER to `PREMIUM` when `membershipLevel` (via the existing `toMembershipLevel`) is \u2265 3, else `STANDARD`.\n- Sets AREA to `METRO` when the owner's locality (via the existing `toLocality`) is a known region \u2014 NSW, VIC, or QLD (checked against the existing `REGION_TIMEZONE` keys) \u2014 else `REGIONAL`.\n\nResults: the two new acceptance tests (`STANDARD_METRO` for a known Sydney/NSW owner, `STANDARD_REGIONAL` for an unknown region) pass, and `./mvnw -o test` reports **BUILD SUCCESS** with all tests green.",
